From c435218d96835b16a2e16df0617485a5fd0058b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:36:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Agent host: surface a Claude steering message as its own
 turn

Steering a Claude session left the message with no representation. The
pending bubble was removed as soon as the queue handed the message to the
SDK, and because the response folded into the running turn, nothing took
its place: the model visibly changed course with no record of why.

Hold the message until the SDK preempts the running turn for it. The
result the SDK emits for the aborted generation completes the turn the
steer interrupted and starts one whose message is the steer, with
queuedMessageId clearing the pending bubble in the same action. The queue
is retargeted so later events and the final completion land in the new
turn. A steer that never runs still clears via steering_consumed.

This is what #318456 did for Copilot, and it matches what M10 already
specified: the ack belongs at model visibility, not queue acceptance.

CONTEXT.md described an SDKUserMessage echo on the event stream as the
visibility signal. The SDK sends no such echo, verified by logging every
user message a live steered turn produced: all were tool_result messages
and the steer appeared only in the on-disk transcript. The intermediate
result is used instead, and the document is corrected.
