From 77530e2bee8cf2aed27a0d5c7454adc21cb8d78b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:28:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Do not render an interrupted turn as failed

Interrupting a turn makes the SDK emit a result of subtype
error_during_execution carrying an internal diagnostic rather than a real
failure, and mapResult turns any such result into a ChatError. Promoting the
steer gives that turn its own bubble, so every steered message rendered an
error above the steer's answer.

The pipeline is the only place that can tell an interruption from a failure,
so the suppression is scoped to the condition the promotion itself uses, and
traces what it drops. An execution error outside a pending steer is untouched.
