From b77eb1cae09a4a26292c1664865122270788116f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:08:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Mint the promoted steering turn, and end it when the
 pipeline aborts

Two corrections to the promotion path.

The promoted turn reused the steering `PendingMessage.id` as its `Turn.id`.
That made one string a pending-message id, an SDK uuid and a protocol turn id
at once. `ChatTurnStarted.queuedMessageId` already carries the link the client
needs to clear the pending bubble, so the turn id can be minted fresh, which is
what the Codex and Copilot paths already do.

The promoted turn also outlived an abort. The client never dispatched this turn
id, so nothing on its side closes it, and the pipeline did not close it either:
the chat was left showing a turn that would run forever. Track the promoted
turn and cancel it when the pipeline aborts or is disposed, clearing it when it
completes normally.

Also corrects three statements in CONTEXT.md that described promotion as
happening on an SDK echo of the steering message. The SDK sends no such echo,
as the same document notes a few lines further down, and the code promotes on
the intermediate result that ends the preempted turn.
